+## Switch runtime boot overlay (M04, 2026-11-12)
+
+The Switch port (root repository, milestone M04) drives the runtime from its own SDL2 main loop and C ABI. These
+changes keep desktop behaviour: `main()` and `run()` take the same steps as before.
+
+| Where | What | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp`, `include/ps2_runtime.h` | `run()` split into `runBegin()` / `runFrame()` / `runEnd()`; `run()` calls them in a loop. The loop's locals live in a file-level `RunLoop`, not in `PS2Runtime` | A host that owns the main loop and the applet lifecycle (the Switch) runs one host frame at a time; `PS2Runtime`'s layout, which the generated code is compiled against, is unchanged |
+| `src/main.cpp`, new `src/launcher.h` | The settings registration, window placement, UI callbacks and post-`loadELF` hook installation are callable as `vcs::launcher::*`; `main()` calls them in the same order. `VCS_LAUNCHER_NO_MAIN` builds the file without `main()`. `setScreenshotDirectory` replaces the folder next to the exe | The Switch core runs upstream's launcher steps, not a copy of them |
+| `ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_host_fs.h` (new), `Kernel/Stubs/MemoryCard.cpp`, `src/settings/settings.cpp` | `ps2x::replaceFile` (rename onto an existing file) and `ps2x::removeTree` (`remove_all`). Elsewhere these are the `std::filesystem` calls; on `__SWITCH__` they move the old file aside / walk the tree, because the Switch SD card fails `rename` onto a file with EEXIST and `remove_all` with EIO (measured on hardware, Switch port M03). Used for vcs.ini, card backup zips, card renames and card format / unformat. A format whose old files cannot be removed now fails with a log line instead of reporting success | Settings could not be saved twice, and a card format left the old saves while reporting a formatted card |
+| `src/game/vcs_stream.cpp`, `vcs_stream.h` | The stream reader thread is kept (was detached) and `stopStreamReader()` finishes its queue and joins it; reads after the stop are refused with a log line | The Switch port releases the folder disc before the process ends; a detached reader could still copy from it |
+| `ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_control.cpp`, `include/runtime/ps2_control.h` | `ps2control::submit(line)`: a command queued as if from the socket, answered through a future | Scripted Switch runs have no socket client |
